                <pb facs="0405" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg309"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p>In answer to your inquiry regarding apple rings (dried pippins), I may say the
                    prime minister sent a circular, dated April 16, 1894, to the allied states, and
                    it is printed by the board of health in their annual for 1894, which is to be
                    had of Mr. Julius Springer, Berlin, N. Menbijon Platz 3.</p>
            </div>
